Back-end pipeline stress (FPU)
==============================

Part of HW_Specific: tests that stress one hardware resource, to study how
interference on it shows up in other partitions. The sizes come from
BENCH_TOOLS/arch_config.h (cache and TLB geometry of the target).

What it tests
-------------

Interference on the execution units at the end of the pipeline (integer units
and FPU), with a minimal memory footprint.

What it does
------------

Two partitions, P1 and P2, one periodic process each.

P1 counts the primes in [1; 10000] (integer division); P2 sums square roots
(floating point). Both processes have a 400 ms period and 200 ms time capacity;
each partition has a 500 ms window in a 1000 ms major frame.

Expected output
---------------

"[p1:...] 1230 primes exist in [1; 10000]" and "[p2:...] SQRT Sum:
437535.218750" (the prime count includes 1, as is_prime() counts it).

Notes
-----

The 400 ms period does not match the partition schedule: some releases fall
outside the partition's window, the hard deadline is missed and the partition
is restarted.

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/PIPELINE/END_PIPE_FP/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/PIPELINE/END_PIPE_FP/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
